#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""board -- the fleet work board CLI, backed by Linear.

Same verbs, flags and text output lines as the mac-collab `board` it replaces,
plus --json, `whoami`, `claim --steal --reason` and `status duplicate --of`.
scripts/linear-board/README.md has the install steps, the frozen contract
table and every environment variable.

Usage:
  board list [--app A] [--team KEY] [--env mac|cloud] [--status S,S] [--severity P0,P1] [--kind K] [--mine SEAT]
             [--label NAME ...] [--search TEXT] [--limit N] [--json]
  board show <id> [--json]
  board file --title T [--app A] [--severity P0..P4] [--desc D | --desc-file PATH|-]
             [--fix F | --fix-file PATH|-] [--label NAME ...]
             [--by SEAT] [--where LOC] [--env Mac|cloud] [--kind K] [--uid U] [--url URL] [--session ID ...]
  board claim <id> --by SEAT [--where LOC] [--env Mac|cloud] [--session ID ...]
             [--steal --reason TEXT] [--comment TEXT]
  board status <id> <open|in_progress|addressed|completed|deployed|wontfix|duplicate|parked>
             [--by SEAT] [--resolution TEXT] [--of <id>] [--session ID ...]
  board comment <id> --by SEAT (--text TEXT | --text-file PATH|-) [--where LOC]
             [--env Mac|cloud] [--session ID ...]
  board label add|remove <id> NAME [--by SEAT]
  board stats
  board whoami

Agent-Sync parity (the hosted server's Linear tools, from catalog/*.json):
  board commands [--search WORD] [--kind read|write] [--json]
  board commands show NAME [--json]
  board run NAME [--arg KEY=VALUE ...] [--args-json JSON|@FILE|-] [--selection FIELDS]
             [--max-chars N] [--idempotency-key KEY] [--session ID ...] [--json]
  board api schema [TYPE] [--field TEXT] [--offset N] [--limit N] [--json]
  board api query DOCUMENT|@FILE|- [--vars JSON|@FILE] [--max-chars N] [--json]
  board api mutation DOCUMENT|@FILE|- [--vars JSON|@FILE] --idempotency-key KEY [--session ID ...]
  board mcp list|show TOOL [--json]
  board mcp call TOOL [--args-json JSON|@FILE|-] [--idempotency-key KEY] [--max-chars N] [--json]

`run` builds the same `AgentSyncNamed` document the hosted server builds and applies its guards:  one
operation, depth 16, 500 fields, no protected or batch mutation roots, only public input fields, and
no edits of claimed:, seat: or stale-claim labels (`board claim` owns those).  A write (a write
command, `api mutation`, or a write `mcp call`) needs a bearer-verified seat and
--idempotency-key:  a retry with the same key returns the first result and never sends it twice, and
an unknown outcome is never replayed automatically.  `mcp` proxies Linear's official MCP server
(https://mcp.linear.app/mcp) with the same app token.

--desc-file, --fix-file and --text-file keep free text out of argv (and so out of
`ps` and shell history).  PATH must be a regular file you own, mode 0600 or 0400,
at most 64 KB of UTF-8;  `-` reads standard input, same cap.  --label, `label` and
`list --label` take only the flat workspace labels needs-owner, ask-capture,
fleet-report and stale-claim.  These are Linear-only (BOARD_BACKEND=mac-collab
refuses them).

Ids: a full board id (32 hex, with or without hyphens), a prefix of 8 or more
hex characters, or a Linear identifier such as AFC-123.

Session ids (AFC-361):  file, claim, status and comment record the session they come from
("sessions: <id>" in the output, a Sessions line in the comment), so a headless resume can find a
seat's session for a topic.  The id is --session, else AGENT_SESSION, else the seat's platform
variable (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, CODEX_THREAD_ID, CURSOR_CONVERSATION_ID, GROK_SESSION_ID,
OPENCODE_SESSION_ID, __MAVIS_RUNTIME_SESSION_ID).  With none, these four verbs exit 2 before they
write.  Grok bots (GROK-BOT, GB-*), MA, JET, WISE and ECHO have one thread with the owner and are
exempt, decided from the verified seat and never from a flag.

Identity:  the run's seat is proven by an admin-minted bearer, verified against
ST-MCP (gr-bearer-verify/1), never parsed from the token and never taken from
the environment (owner direction 2026-10-26:  the bearer identifies the agent,
on the server and the Mac alike;  there is no identity picker).  A trusted
launcher binds the run to SIMPLE_BOARD_BEARER_LOCATOR, a non-secret
FOLDER:KEY_NAME location;  with no locator the write verbs refuse and reads
run without a seat.  The Linear side is a Linear app that mints its own token by OAuth client credentials
(design section 2).  Each seat has its own app, named for the seat bot (CLAUDE
signs as "Claude"), when its <SEAT>_LINEAR_CLIENT_ID and _SECRET are in Infisical Fleet-OPS /linear;
a seat with no app yet, and every read without a bearer, uses the shared
"Fleet" app.  Each app has its own token, stored in Infisical (CACHE_<SEAT>).  The seat comes only from the
verified bearer, which the five write verbs require and the read verbs do not.
The shared app cannot tell seats apart, so every issue and comment this CLI writes
starts with a seat tag line ([CLAUDE·6db9ee77]), with a seat app too.  A seat
app's writes are refused when Linear names another app as the viewer
(swapped credentials).  A claim is a claimed:<TAG> label on the issue;
seat:<TAG> labels only say who reported or touched it (the import put them on
reporters too), so they are never read as a claim.  A write needs the
bearer-verified seat and nothing else.  BOARD_BACKEND=mac-collab runs the old board CLI
instead for reads (rollback);  it never carries a write, which needs the bearer-verified seat.

Stdlib only, so cloud seats, the Grok Bot VM and BotFleet containers can run
it from any AI-Fleet-Coordinator checkout: python3 scripts/linear-board/board.
"""
